    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The frai-core test suite is now fully passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**Two fixes were needed:**\n\n1. **Export governance constants** (`packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`):\n   - The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n2. **Fix toxicityMetric function** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`):\n   - The function was receiving the references array as a second parameter from `runEvaluations`, but was treating it as banned terms\n   - Changed the signature to ignore the references parameter and always use the default banned terms\n   - This fixed the toxicity score calculation from returning 0 to correctly returning 1 (no toxicity detected)\n\n**Test Results:**\n- \u2705 All 28 tests now pass across 8 test files\n- \u2705 All existing public exports remain working\n\nThe changes are staged and ready to commit.",
